      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I will strongly argue that the expansion of executive privilege constitutes a dangerous erosion of checks and balances because it undermines the Founders' deliberate design for transparent governance. By treating this privilege as an unfettered power shielded from congressional or judicial review, modern presidents risk insulating bad governance, corruption, or foreign policy blunders from necessary public accountability. This position centers on overstepping the narrowly defined \"need for confidentiality\" for national security, arguing instead that legislative oversight is a non-delegable duty essential to a functioning democracy.",
