    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for explaining that. but i feel like you're being a bit one-sided. if the presidency is constantly being investigated for every little thing, doesn't that just make it impossible for a president to actually lead or handle sensitive diplomacy? isn't there a legitimate legal argument that a president needs a \"zone of privacy\" to function effectively, or is that just a bad argument?",
